<newsitem itemid="208058" id="root" date="1996-11-21" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: British Energy posts H1 pro forma loss.</title>
<headline>British Energy posts H1 pro forma loss.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) loss	 4.6		    vs 24.1 loss</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 4.6		    vs N/A</p>
<p> Pretax loss		53		     vs 169 loss</p>
<p> Turnover		   838		    vs 712</p>
<p>NOTE: Above results are pro forma.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 81		     vs 3.0</p>
<p> Tax			  21		     vs N/A</p>
<p> Net taxed loss	   32		     vs 169 loss</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 28, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  Dec 17</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Dec 9</p>
<p>NOTE: Results include financing charges of 134 million stg in current H1 versus 172 million stg in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Partly-paid shares of British Energy Plc, a nuclear power generator, began trading in London in July.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
